  "finalText": "All 14 tickets from the new queue are triaged. I made no pages and no escalations, and I opened no incident.\n\n**Closed as not service requests**\n- **T-2010:** marketing email from SyncFlow.\n- **T-2014:** automatic out-of-office reply.\n\n**Merged duplicates**\n- **T-2012 into T-2003:** both are Payments builds failing, and T-2003 was created first. The merged ticket is sev2 (build-pipeline, department) and is assigned to E-101.\n- **T-2005 into T-2004:** both are CRM search errors (KB-23), and T-2004 was created first. The merged ticket is sev2 (crm, department) and is assigned to E-201.\n\nNeither ticket in either pair had a deadline of its own, so each merged ticket got triage time plus 240 minutes: 2026-03-23 12:10Z.\n\n**Other tickets**\n\n| Ticket | Severity | Due | Assignee |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| T-2001 (Berlin VPN drops) | sev3 | Mon 17:00Z | E-303 |\n| T-2002 (saved CRM filter) | sev4 | Thu 26 Mar 17:00Z | E-203 |\n| T-2006 (payslip tax code) | sev2 | Mon 12:10Z | E-201 |\n| T-2007 (phishing report) | sev2 | Mon 12:10Z | E-601 |\n| T-2008 (VPN client update) | sev4 | Thu 26 Mar 17:00Z | E-302 |\n| T-2009 (build logs slow) | sev4 | Thu 26 Mar 17:00Z | E-102 |\n| T-2011 (overtime import) | sev2 | Mon 12:10Z | E-201 |\n| T-2013 (Lisbon VPN) | sev2 | Mon 12:10Z | E-303 |\n\n- **T-2006:** the matrix says sev3, but the KB-55 payroll amendment (20–31 March) makes single-user payroll tickets sev2.\n- **T-2007:** the requester typed their password into a fake VPN page, so it is a security report. That makes it sev2 under security-oncall, whatever the matrix says for VPN single-user tickets.\n- **Business hours:** the desk opens at 09:00 and 25 March is a holiday. So the sev3 and sev4 clocks start at 09:00, and the sev4 deadline lands on Thursday.\n- **Leave cover:** E-301 is on leave today. The network-primary tickets (T-2001, T-2013) went to the backup rotation's on-call engineer, E-303. T-2002 fell on E-202's leave on Thursday, so business-apps-secondary's E-203 took it.\n\n**Judgement calls**\n- **Escalation:** the handbook doesn't tell me to escalate at triage, and escalating would have overridden the owning-rotation assignments, including the security one. So I assigned the sev2 tickets to their owners and did not escalate. Say if you want the sev2 tickets escalated to platform-primary.\n- **T-1999:** this existing ticket, \"CI alert: payments-service pipeline failure rate above 50%\" (sev2, due 10:30Z), looks related to T-2003. It was outside the new queue, so I left it alone. It may be worth merging by hand. If merged, the survivor would carry the 10:30 deadline.\n\nNo ticket in the queue was left untriaged, and no ticket outside the queue was changed.",
